Translation patch: `From<Vec<(N, V)>> for Params` (panic message)

Change: `panic!("Redefinition of named parameter `{}'", String::from_utf8_lossy(&name))` becomes `panic!("Redefinition of named parameter")`.
Why: Formatting goes through `fmt` and `String::from_utf8_lossy`, which Aeneas does not model (as in patch 47).
Behaviour: Identical except for the text of the panic message: it panics in exactly the same cases.

diff --git a/src/params.rs b/src/params.rs
index 6dc7889..7a08265 100644
--- a/src/params.rs
+++ b/src/params.rs
@@ -202,10 +202,7 @@ where
         for (name, value) in x.into_iter() {
             let name: Vec<u8> = name.into();
             if crate::sql_trusted::params_map_contains_key(&map, &name) {
-                panic!(
-                    "Redefinition of named parameter `{}'",
-                    String::from_utf8_lossy(&name)
-                );
+                panic!("Redefinition of named parameter");
             } else {
                 crate::sql_trusted::params_map_insert(&mut map, name, Value::from(value));
             }
